Sir Mark,

=20

Further to my Formal Request of 19 May 2026, I write with a supplementary s=
ubmission to the existing Metropolitan Police criminal referral file CCR-650=
1-26-0100-000.

=20

The Formal Request of 19 May 2026 set out the perjury allegation in respect=
 of the sworn $0 valuation of 19 February 2024 contrasted with the SEC Defin=
itive Proxy Statement valuation of approximately $565,000 of 16 January 2024=
.

=20

This supplementary submission places before the Service the wider network w=
ithin which the Oxus discrepancy arose: the documented relationship between =
Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor and Kenes Rakishev, the controlling shareholder o=
f Oxus Acquisition Corp; the structural function of the Oxus and Tavia SPAC =
vehicles; and the documented intermediary role of David Stern between Andrew=
 Mountbatten-Windsor and Jeffrey Epstein. Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor was arr=
ested on 19 February 2026 on suspicion of misconduct in public office during=
 his tenure as UK Special Representative for International Trade and Investm=
ent.

=20

The Analytical Briefing and Document Index attached set out the documentary=
 record. The exhibits NZ-L-01 through NZ-L-11 are primary source materials d=
rawn from US federal court records, congressional records, SEC EDGAR, the US=
 DOJ Epstein files released January 2025, and published investigative journa=
lism.

=20

The relevance to the perjury allegation under file CCR-6501-26-0100-000 is =
structural rather than direct. The sworn $0 valuation of 19 February 2024 wa=
s made by a director of an entity controlled by a named non-executive chairm=
an whose network has been the subject of US congressional investigation, US =
federal court litigation, and an SEC whistleblower submission (reference TCR=
 17284-760-060-567 of 9 October 2024, naming IRS:CI Special Agent Robert McG=
arry as the assigned federal agent).

=20

The supplementary submission is provided for completeness within the existi=
ng criminal referral file. The asks of 19 May 2026 =E2=80=94 record, assess, and p=
rovide a reasoned written response within 14 days =E2=80=94 remain.

=20

Respectfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person | BV20D01752 | Veritas Numquam Perit

=20

---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
---------------------------------------------

Nadia Zahmoul =20

Claimant =E2=80=94 Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Justice & HMCTS =20

